 Self-Employment Contributions Act, as amended (26 U.S.C. 1201-1203). The Social Security Act Amendments of 1956, approved August 1, 1956, increased the rate of tax applicable to wages paid and taxable years beginning after December 31, 1956, to provide for disability insurance.\\n5) Taxes on carriers and their employees under the Railroad Retirement Tax Act, as amended (26 U.S.C. 3201-3233).\\n6) Tax on employer of 4 or more under the Federal Unemployment Tax Act, as amended (26 U.S.C. 3301-3308); with respect to services performed before January 1, 1956, the tax was imposed on employers of 8 or more. Remaining footnotes on following page.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [7, 11, 156, 39], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"February 1960\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1047, 24, 1057, 39], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"3\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [387, 65, 685, 81], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"BUDGET RECEIPTS AND EXPENDITURES\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [364, 113, 702, 128], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"Footnotes to Table 1 - (Continued)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [22, 155, 508, 250], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"Through 1953, contributions to the Railroad Unemployment Insurance Administration Fund were carried in the daily Treasury statement as miscellaneous receipts, while the 1961 Budget document, Special Analysis G, includes them in employment taxes in 1952. Beginning 1954, the contributions are credited direct to the trust account. For amounts of the contributions included in budget receipts, see \\\"Treasury Bulletin\\\" for February 1954, page 7.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [21, 249, 499, 278], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"In the 1961 Budget document, Special Analysis C, taxes not otherwise classified are included in miscellaneous receipts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [19, 278, 485, 305], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"9/ Beginning 1957, includes collections under increased rates in the Highway Revenue Act of 1956 (see footnote 14).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [19, 304, 509, 474], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"Figures shown include adjustments (see footnote 11) as follows: In January, decreases in income tax of $82 million withheld and $7 million withheld by the Trust Fund; in April, $37 million to Federal Old-Age and Survivors Insurance Trust Fund and $5 million to Federal Disability Insurance Trust Fund; in April, increase in income tax withheld of $129 million and decreases in income tax not withheld of $12 million; in June, transfers of $114 million to Federal Old-Age and Survivors Insurance Trust Fund and $11 million to Federal Disability Insurance Trust Fund; in June, increase in income tax withheld of $138 million and decreases in income tax not withheld of $14 million, and in transfers of $111 million to Federal Old-Age and Survivors Insurance Trust Fund and $13 million to Federal Disability Insurance Trust Fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [11, 475, 501, 622], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"Amounts appropriated to the Federal Old-Age and Survivors Insurance Trust Fund are equivalent to the amounts of taxes collected and deposited for old-age insurance (42 U.S.C. 401 (a)). Beginning January 1951, the amounts transferred currently for appropriation to the trust fund are based on estimates of old-age insurance tax receipts made by the Secretary of the Treasury pursuant to the provisions of Sec. 201 (a) of the Social Security Act, as amended (42 U.S.C. 401 (a)), and are adjusted in later transfers on the basis of wage and salary earnings. All records maintained in the Social Security Administration. The amount of old-age insurance tax refunds is reimbursed to the general fund by the trust fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [12, 621, 487, 655], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"12/ The Federal Disability Insurance Trust Fund was established by the Social Security Act Amendments of 1956, approved August 1, 1956\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [583, 158, 1039, 278], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"(42 U.S.C. 401 (b)). The act appropriated to the trust fund amounts equivalent to specified percentages of the wages and self-employment income, respectively, which are taxed for old-age insurance, and provided that the amounts appropriated should be transferred from time to time to the trust fund on the same basis as transfers to the Federal Old-Age and Survivors Insurance Trust Fund. Rates of tax were increased by the percentages appropriated to the Federal Disability Insurance Trust Fund, the increase being applicable to wages paid and taxable years beginning after December 31, 1956.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [549, 276, 1053, 360], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"13/ Excludes the Government's contribution for creditable military service (45 U.S.C. 228c-1 (n)). Beginning 1952, amounts are appropriated to the Railroad Retirement Account equal to the amount of taxes under the Railroad Retirement Tax Act deposited in the Treasury, less refunds, during each fiscal year (65 Stat. 222 and 66 Stat. 371), and transfers are made currently.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [549, 359, 1052, 545], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"The Highway Revenue Act of 1956, approved June 29, 1956 (23 U.S.C. 173) established a Highway Trust Fund from which are to be made, as provided by appropriation acts, Federal-aid highway expenditures after June 30, 1956, and also are to be made, as provided by appropriations, this fund amounts equivalent to specified percentages of receipts from certain excise taxes on motor fuels, motor vehicles, tires and tubes, and use of certain vehicles, and provided that the amounts appropriated should be transferred currently to the trust fund on the basis of estimates by the Secretary of the Treasury with proper adjustments to be made in subsequent transfers. The use tax was imposed by the act. Rates were increased for the other taxes. Previous to the fiscal year 1957-58, proportional excise tax receipts were included in net budget receipts, and Federal-aid highway expenditures were included in budget expenditures.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [549, 545, 982, 562], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"15/ Interest on refunds is included in expenditures in Table 2.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [550, 559, 1025, 590], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"16/ Transfers reduced by $300 million to correct those made earlier on basis of estimates (see footnote 11).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [549, 588, 1017, 604], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"17 Net of reimbursement of $83 million from the Federal Old-Age and\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [549, 603, 710, 627], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"Survivors Insurance\\n* Less than $500,000.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [366, 772, 705, 789], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"Footnotes to Table 2 - (Continued)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [2, 821, 324, 834], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"Footnotes 1 through 3 follow Table 2 on page 4.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [4, 834, 465, 931], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"The 1959 figures in the Bulletin differ from those in the 1961 Budget document because of a reclassification in the latter by which military assistance under the Mutual Security program in the amount of $2,340 million is shifted from \\\"Funds appropriated to the President\\\" to \\\"Defense Department, military functions,\\\" and $8 million is shifted from \\\"State Department\\\" to \\\"Funds appropriated to the President.\\\" Monthly figures in the Bulletin\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [5, 931, 471, 966], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"5/ Totals include allowance for contingencies of $75 million for 1960 and $200 million for 1961.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [2, 963, 470, 994], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"6/ Includes unclassified expenditure transfers until these have been distributed in final fiscal year figures.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 21, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [576, 823, 1035, 857], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"Beginning 1955, consists of net expenditures of the Postal Fund, reflecting the change in classification of Post Office transactions to a public enterprise, revolving fund basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 22, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [576, 857, 960, 878], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"8/ Reported on an accrual basis effective June 30, 1955.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 23, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [575, 874, 944, 890], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"9/ Consists of Federal payment and loans and advances.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 24, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [572, 889, 1018, 908], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"10/ Includes $1,375 million additional subscription to the Inter-\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 25, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [572, 905, 1013, 929], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"national Moetary Fund pursuant to Public Law 86-48, approved June 17, 1959.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 26, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [578, 929, 730, 945], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"Less than $500,000.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 27, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [24, 14, 31, 27], \"page_id\": 18}], \"content\": \"\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [893, 6, 1068, 40], \"page_id\": 18}], \"content\": \"Treasury Bulletin\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [401, 60, 702, 74], \"page_id\": 18}], \"content\": \"BUDGET RECEIPTS AND EXPENDITURES\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [377, 108, 724, 126], \"page_id\": 18}], \"content\": \"Table 2.- Expenditures by Agencies\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [471, 132, 628, 145], \"page_id\": 18}], \"content\": \"(In millions of dollars)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [24, 151, 1074, 578], \"page_id\": 18}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Fiscal year or month</th><th>Total</th><th>Legislative branch</th><th>Judiciary</th><th>Executive Office of the President</th><th>Funds appropriated to the President</th><th>Independent offices</th><th>General Services Administration</th><th>Housing and Home Finance Agency</th><th>Agriculture Department</th><th>Commerce Department</th></tr><tr><td>1953</td><td>74,274</td><td>61</td><td>27</td><td>9</td><td>5,782</td><td>6,905</td><td>1,107</td><td>385</td><td>3,217</td><td>1,063</td></tr><tr><td>1954</td><td>67,772</td><td>59</td><td>28</td><td>9</td><td>5,282</td><td>6,479 1/2</td><td>806</td><td>-615</td><td>2,915</td><td>1,00