16, 1369], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"Differences between the amounts of internal revenue reported by the Internal Revenue Service as collections for given periods and the amounts reported in Treasury statements as budget receipts for the same periods are attributable to the fact that some collections were included in the respective reports. Tax payments are included in budget receipts when they are reported as credits to the account of the Treasurer of the United States. Prior to July 1954, they were included in Internal Revenue Service collection reports after the returns to which they applied had been received in internal revenue offices. Under procedure begun in 1950 with withheld income tax and old-age insurance taxes and in 1953 with social security tax, returns to the States and many excise taxes are paid currently into Treasury depositories and the depository receipts, as evidence of such payments, are attached to quarterly returns to the Internal Revenue Service.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [553, 992, 1041, 1053], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"Under this procedure, the payments are included in budget receipts in the month in which the depository receipts are issued to the taxpayers. Revised accounting procedures effective July 1, 1954, extended the same practice to Internal Revenue Service collection receipts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [556, 1058, 1023, 1123], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"Monthly figures include social security tax on self-employment income, which is levied and collected as part of the individual income tax. Fiscal year figures exclude this tax, on the basis of estimates (see footnote 3), and it is included under \\\"Old-age and disability insurance.\\\"\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [552, 1127, 1039, 1204], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"3/ In Internal Revenue Service reports current collections are not separated as to type of tax; the breakdown shown for fiscal years is based on estimates made in accordance with provisions of Sec. 201 of the Social Security Act, as amended (42 U.S.C. 401), for transfer of tax receipts to the trust funds (see \\\"Budget Receipts and Expenditures,\\\" Table 1).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [554, 1207, 1057, 1260], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"Beginning with the fiscal year 1955, collections shown include undis- tributed depositary receipts and unapplied collections. For excise taxes these receipts are included in the total only. Total collections include \\\"Taxes not otherwise classified.\\\"\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [556, 1262, 1040, 1337], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"Budget receipts for 1956 were reduced by $3,566 thousand represent-ing tax collections transferred to the Government of Guam pursuant to the act approved August 1, 1950 (64 Stat. 392), but this amount was included in collections reported by the Internal Revenue Service. Beginning with 1957, such collections are excluded also in Internal Revenue Service reports.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [552, 1342, 1029, 1353], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"6/ Detail is reported by quarters beginning with the fiscal year 1956.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [38, 37, 67, 58], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"58\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [911, 26, 1087, 56], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"Treasury Bulletin\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [424, 77, 675, 95], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"INTERNAL REVENUE COLLECTIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [242, 126, 857, 155], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"INTERNAL REVENUE COLLECTIONS BY PRINCIPAL SOURCES\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [96, 161, 986, 1323], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [219, 1327, 880, 1360], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"* Beginning with the fiscal year 1955, includes undistributed depository receipts and unapplied collections. The whole amount of such receipts for excise taxes is included under \\\"Other excise taxes.\\\"\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [949, 1367, 986, 1380], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"B-165-0\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [95, 1367, 256, 1380], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"Office of the Secretary of the Treasury\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1024, 31, 1045, 48], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"59\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [4, 18, 154, 45], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"January 1960\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [431, 68, 617, 87], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"MONETARY STATISTICS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [381, 112, 689, 138], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"Table 1.- Money in Circulation\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [363, 140, 698, 162], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"(In millions of dollars except per capita figures)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1, 162, 1052, 638], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>End of fiscal year or month</th><th>Tot